@@ -2418,3 +2418,98 @@ Bug Fixes:
   open each time. After many coprocesses,
   iTerm2 could run out of open files and fail
   to create new sessions.
+OmniTerm turns window close and quit actions into
+hide actions while keeping terminal sessions alive.
+OmniTerm removes the compact proxy icon and uses a teal window border so its
+terminal windows are visually distinct from regular iTerm2 windows.
+OmniTerm supports exactly one terminal window, redirects new-window requests
+to tabs, and always displays its tab bar.
+Escape hides OmniTerm's terminal window, and Control-Option-Space toggles it.
+OmniTerm adds a native agent scheduler and the omni
+CLI for interactive Codex and Claude run tabs.
+Agent timeouts now apply only outside the ten newest
+run tabs, keeping retained agents interactive.
+The agent dashboard now has responsive cards, colors,
+mouse actions, details, and live run history.
+Agent files now live in ~/.omni and reload live.
+Recent runs can resume in a new terminal tab.
+The agent editor now matches the dashboard with
+cards, color, progress, preview, and review views.
+Escape now reaches the terminal. A fast double
+Escape hides the OmniTerm window.
+Omni starts first and unpinned, while stale tabs
+and unwanted startup shells are cleaned up.
+Agent creation can discover a project from a path.
+Scheduling timezone is now a global setting.
+The omni CLI now has noun-first agent commands,
+full help, JSON output, and compatibility aliases.
+Managed Claude and Codex tabs now keep their colors
+even when OmniTerm inherited a NO_COLOR setting.
+Managed agent TUIs now receive terminal resize
+signals and redraw at the new pane dimensions.
+Startup now removes inherited placeholder shells
+and late-exiting Terminal Python tabs reliably.
+OmniTerm now stays hidden throughout app launch,
+including window restoration and dashboard setup.
+The agent wizard now has clickable provider and
+model pickers and a non-scrolling path picker.
+Prompt editors use Enter to save and Command-Enter
+for new lines; blank names are generated smartly.
+Agent details now show wrapped system and startup
+prompt previews beside schedule and run history.
+Dashboard prompt previews are now keyboard-focusable
+and clickable, with a full scrollable prompt viewer.
+Workspace completion no longer exits when terminal
+cursor-visibility control is unavailable.
+The menu-bar now opens native OmniTerm settings
+for its shortcut, login, behavior, and agents.
+Settings and reopen requests never restore or show
+windows during OmniTerm background startup.
+The menu-bar icon now matches OmniTerm's O-and-
+cursor mark in the native monochrome template style.
+Secondary launches no longer replace the active
+scheduler socket or break dashboard commands.
+Wizard pickers no longer inherit dashboard polling
+timeouts and exit while waiting for user input.
+OmniTerm now bundles and globally registers an MCP
+agent scheduler for Claude Code and Codex.
+The omni MCP offers agent CRUD, schedule previews,
+run control, resume, diagnostics, and JSON results.
+Agent retention now rejects zero or negative
+durations unless retention is explicitly off.
+Agent editing now stays in one inline form.
+Left and Right move between its fields.
+Choices appear below the active field.
+Workspace Tab completion now behaves like cd.
+Tab descends folders; Enter accepts the path.
+Modified Return inserts prompt line breaks.
+Claude permission choices include auto-mode.
+Dashboard keys now bypass profile remapping.
+Left always returns to the agent list.
+Only focused Run now Enter or a click runs.
+Replacement runs now tolerate pending run rows
+whose process identifiers are not assigned yet.
+Agent schedules now use calendar-style repeat
+count, period, and contextual on/at controls.
+Aligned hourly, daily, weekly, and monthly
+recurrence is supported by the native scheduler.
+Short months clamp and later restore month days.
+
+OmniTerm distribution:
+- Adds public release packaging, installer/MCP setup, licensing credits, and
+  correct GPL-3.0-or-later bundle metadata for the modified iTerm2 distribution.
+Agent tabs now close as soon as their run ends,
+for any reason, including a failed start.
+Agents launched at login find claude and codex
+through the login shell’s PATH, and a start
+failure is recorded in the run history.
+Runs left behind by a dead runner are now failed
+instead of staying in “starting” forever.
+A malformed or null scheduler request, such as
+listing runs with no agent, no longer crashes
+OmniTerm.
+The scheduler no longer runs on the main thread,
+so a busy tab cannot delay it, and it cannot slow
+down drawing.
+An agent file with an invalid schedule is now
+skipped instead of crashing OmniTerm at launch.
